HHIISSTTOORRYY
       glibc 2.1.  POSIX.1‐2001.

       This is part of the UNIX 98 pseudoterminal support, see ppttss(4).

       Historical systems implemented this function via a set‐user‐ID helper
       binary called "pt_chown".  glibc on Linux before glibc 2.33 could do so
       as well, in order to support configurations with only BSD
       pseudoterminals; this support has been removed.  On modern systems this
       is either a no‐op —with permissions configured on pty allocation, as is
       the case on Linux— or an iiooccttll(2).

